    "updated_at": "2019-04-18T02:27:46Z",
    "body": "I definitely agree that YAML is a good option.\r\n\r\n> I'd be happy with either YAML or TOML, I'd suggest maybe allowing the user to decide which configuration format they prefer and automatically use the correct parser?\r\n\r\nWe could certainly bake in support for both, but we'd end up writing documentation for one or the other, really. I think that providing first-class support to both could make for a confusing time documenting and sharing configs among users.\r\nI'd personally prefer for convention over configuration in this case, but that's just me.\r\n\r\nThat said, I could certainly be persuaded to use YAML instead.\r\n\r\n> In addition, please stop throwing your trash in my home!\r\n\r\nI didn't realize this was a problem! 😆\r\nAbsolutely, that's a good idea to put the config files in `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME` or `~/.config`.\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
